  "implementation": [
    "The existing native engine controls now enter through current canonical intent parsing, protected Store source/Device/key/member authority, original physical ownership and one shared-ledger attempt. A separate exact Gates plan admits only its matching action, Stream set, Connection and revision. It cannot borrow an initial offer or issue a negotiation counteroffer.",
    "Hold supports default endpoint recvonly plus explicit sendonly/recvonly/inactive; resume clears hold/pause and preserves independent mute. Mute/unmute require explicit exact logical Streams. Gate controls change no negotiated codec, physical handle or Connection generation. Metadata-only status is not media readiness.",
    "The actual returned engine states become a consuming captured receipt with exact targets, action, revision, binding and gate validation. Record result/effect/journal and matching live-generation stream revision/latest partial observation commit atomically. Replay preserves original result without resetting newer controls; receipt retry holds no old command readers and never calls Core again.",
    "Both signature algorithms exercise actual decoded duplex PCMU, source mute with receive preserved, default directional hold, reverse directional hold, inactive hold, mute while paused, resume while still muted, explicit unmute, original logical replay, foreign-peer refusal without reserving an operation, stale/unknown refusal without an effect, and HTTP native-control refusal.",
    "An actual muted PCMU-to-PCMA replacement keeps publication silent while decoded receive uses the new codec. A fresh unmute restores decoded publication through the new handle/generation. The original mute receipt retains its old binding observation and cannot reset the newer live binding.",
    "A forced completion-journal failure preserves the same captured actual mute while an independent public role writer and operation cancellation proceed. Recovery finalizes one original effect without another Core call; later unmute and old-result replay preserve the newer state.",
    "Both algorithms offer PCMA before PCMU while the current accepted Session profile permits only PCMU. Actual signed answers select the offered usable PCMU fallback and advertise the current intersection. A PCMA-only offer refuses before any native effect while both existing decoded routes continue.",
    "Current regressions cover actual first-readiness/lifecycle and codec publication, independent Connection end preserving other Session media, captured end recovery, codec/capability/quality updates, audio/video/data selectors and shared native/HTTP Session controls. No new implementation is credited to these existing paths."
